  "mathematical_review": "ENTIRE frozen 299-line source, all private finite-dimensional/quotient and recurrence helpers, genuine jet/multiplication/projection definitions and all FOUR complete written BP proofs plus the transparent definition node reviewed. Actual finite jets are literal whole ideal quotients R/(I+m^q), with finite complex dimension proved from the genuine formal coefficient truncation theorem. Multiplication by the actual pivot variable is well-defined between consecutive jets, and the true whole colon identity gives injectivity by actual numerator membership. The literal fibre quotient projection is actually surjective; expanding its kernel into I+(e)+m^(q+1) gives exactly the whole multiplication range, with no exact-sequence certificate input. Genuine rank-nullity therefore gives the precise finite complex dimension recurrence. For ANY finite pivot-fixed whole family, projection of a real ideal-plus-power representation, actual projection-kernel divisibility, coefficient-shift power reflection and cancellation of the nonzero actual formal variable internally prove EVERY whole colon identity, without homogeneity or incoming regularity. Each original generator differs from its actual pivot shadow by a true multiple of e, giving the WHOLE equality of their ideals after adjoining (e). The original ideal with disclosed all-order colons and its literal pivot-shadow extension therefore have identical fibre-quotient ideals and genuine rank recurrences. Induction from the actual zero jet proves equality of ALL whole jet dimensions and hence the actual HS profile. The shadow span is an ideal in the SAME ambient n-variable formal ring, not the lower-dimensional quotient by e. Finally an original analytic J/j/b fixes ONE canonical normalized H before all current-order bounds and all HS orders; the preceding strict-symbol producer internally supplies its actual formal colons under those natural retained vertex-order bounds. Whole original-to-formal jet equivalence identifies the independently named normalized analytic HS value with its Taylor extension, yielding precisely equality with the SAME H shadow-span profile. No original SOURCE profile identification, shear theorem, converse or relative-centre criterion is inserted.",
